<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI14-QA1-RBQA-F001>
  triage:status "scope-mismatch" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:resolutionGuidance "HOLD -- do not implement either 'remove UDS' or 'remove TCP' as previously guided (both directions were dispatched and retracted). docs/requirements.md REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-001 states: 'Unix same-host clients use HTTP over UDS and may use HTTP over loopback TCP; Windows same-host clients use HTTP over loopback TCP only' and explicitly requires 'Unix/Windows parity requires equivalent local HTTP request/response tests: UDS plus loopback TCP on Unix and loopback TCP on Windows.' This means concurrent UDS+TCP-loopback binding on Unix is the DOCUMENTED, REQUIRED contract, not dead/violating infrastructure. The finding's premise ('dead/unreferenced-by-any-client production infrastructure kept alive, not removed', 'Single-receive-path boundary violation') conflicts with this requirement and needs re-triage against REQ-CORE-TRANSPORT-001 before any dispatch. Client-side (atm-daemon-client) currently resolving only via local_http_record_path may itself be the real gap (missing UDS-path client support), not the server binding both listeners. Needs fresh triage, not implementation." .
